-- title:
--   Finite locally free kernel from geometric fibre degrees
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative Noetherian ring and let $\varphi = (\varphi_0, \varphi_1)$ be a pair of formal power series in two variables over $B$, that is, an element of `Series B` $= \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to B[\![x_0,x_1]\!]$. Assume that each $\varphi_i$ has vanishing constant coefficient, and that there is an $N \in \mathbb{N}$ with $x_i^{N}$ in the ideal generated by $\varphi_0, \varphi_1$ for both $i$. Let $d \in \mathbb{N}$ and assume that for every algebraically closed field $\kappa$ and every ring homomorphism $f \colon B \to \kappa$ the quotient $\kappa[\![x_0,x_1]\!] / (f\varphi_0, f\varphi_1)$, where $f$ is applied coefficientwise, has dimension exactly $d$ as a $\kappa$-vector space. The conclusion is `HasKernelOfDegree φ d`, which unfolds to three assertions about the kernel algebra $A = B[\![x_0,x_1]\!] / (\varphi_0,\varphi_1)$: it is a finite $B$-module, it is a projective $B$-module, and for every field $\kappa$ — no longer assumed algebraically closed — and every ring homomorphism $f \colon B \to \kappa$, the $\kappa$-algebra $\kappa[\![x_0,x_1]\!] / (f\varphi_0, f\varphi_1)$ has $\kappa$-dimension $d$.
--
--   This is the passage from a fibrewise dimension hypothesis over geometric points to finite local freeness of constant degree over the base, in the form required by the Čerednik–Drinfel'd formal module package. It is used in the proof that the formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module attached to the edge structure constants has height four.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_hasKernelOfDegree_of_X_pow_mem_of_forall_finrank_eq_of_isAlgClosed.lean

